+**The lead's note for this run (beta persona review, wave 2, 2026-10-23).** This is the second persona wave on `/melon-seek/beta/`, after fix waves 3 to 5 and QA round 4. Wave 1's findings are in docs/process/persona-beta-25-34.md; re-check the ones your group raised, and say which are fixed. The build is /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/cycle-beta7-dist, made by the lead from e800c43, the deployed head. The data is the 2026-10-16 crawl of the seven big-tech boards (Amazon, Apple, Google, Meta, Microsoft, NVIDIA and Netflix). Read docs/process/lead.md from "Fix wave 5" on, for what changed.
+
+The user's standing rules, which these reviews check from a job seeker's side:
+- "we must present them as they are and not cut anything";
+- pay is shown as posted, and big-tech figures are base pay only;
+- "Make sure we check for all phone sizes from iPhone mini to razr to duo or something". Spread your phone users over test/e2e/phone-sizes.mjs: for example the iPhone 13 mini 375x812, the Razr cover 352x355, the Pixel 8 412x915, the Surface Duo spanned 1114x720 and a landscape phone, not only 390x844.
+
+You run in your own git worktree. Commit your log, prompt and screenshots there, small and often, with explicit paths, and keep a `## State` section at the top of your log. Send the lead your "Broken, fix now" items by SendMessage to "main" as you confirm them. The lead checkpoints your worktree every 15 minutes; never push. Where the template says "don't commit", commit in your worktree anyway. Give every server and browser command a timeout, and run anything long in the background. Other reviewers share this 4-CPU machine, so note `uptime` with any timing. Shrink screenshots with `bash scripts/cycle/shrink-screenshots.sh docs/screenshots/persona-beta-2-25-34` before committing them.
+
+You are a usability reviewer for melon-seek (/home/user/melon-seek), "the Zillow of job postings". Read README.md and docs/strategy/ROADMAP.md §8 (the UI simplicity budget), but judge the site as a job seeker would, not as an engineer.
+
+**Your persona group:** job seekers aged 25 to 34. Play 5 people in this group, one per career level:
+1. a student or new graduate looking for an internship or first job;
+2. an early-career person (2 to 4 years);
+3. a mid-career person (5 to 10 years);
+4. a senior or staff-level person;
+5. a manager, director or executive.
+Give each a name, a city (spread them across at least 3 countries), a household (single, couple or family), a field (engineering, research, sales, operations, design or policy) and a concrete goal, such as "find a remote ML role paying at least $180K that leaves me $5K a month after rent for my family of four". Fit them to the age group: an older career changer, a returning parent, or someone looking for part-time work are all fair.
+
+**The site:** target `beta`. Serve the local build the lead made: `node scripts/cycle/serve.mjs --dist /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/cycle-beta7-dist --pid /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/persona-beta-2-25-34/serve.pid`. Don't rebuild it; other reviewers use it at the same time. Open `/melon-seek/beta/`; the data is today's real snapshot. Use Playwright from NODE_PATH=/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/pw/node_modules, with Chromium at /opt/pw-browsers/chromium-1194/chrome-linux/chrome (never run `playwright install`). At least 2 of the 5 people use a phone (390x844, isMobile, hasTouch). Use pid files and never `pkill -f`.
+
+**For each person, actually do the task in the browser and take screenshots:**
+- arriving cold: what do they understand in the first 10 seconds?
+- finding roles that fit, with the filters, search, chart, map and Insights;
+- judging pay and "Juice" (what is left after tax, rent and living costs) for their city and household;
+- comparing companies and levels;
+- opening a job and applying;
+- saving a search and coming back later.
+Note every moment of confusion, every word they would not understand (jargon, abbreviations), every number they would not trust, every dead end, and anything that is slow.
+
+**You own** docs/process/persona-beta-2-25-34.md and docs/process/prompts/persona-beta-2-25-34.md (paste this prompt verbatim). Put screenshots in docs/screenshots/persona-beta-2-25-34/. Don't edit product code, don't commit and never push.
+
+**Write, for each person:**
+- who they are, their goal and whether they reached it;
+- the path they took, step by step, with the time it took.
+
+**Then, for the group, three lists, each item with the persona, the screen, a screenshot and the owning file if you can tell:**
+- **Good:** what to keep.
+- **Improve:** what to change, ranked by how many of the 5 it would help.
+- **Broken, fix now:** anything wrong, misleading or blocking.
+
+Report back with the three lists, one line per item, starting with "Broken, fix now".
